      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Zeeshan will briefly explain what UPnP is all about, followed by an introduction to &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.gupnp.org/&#34;&gt;GUPnP API&lt;/a&gt; with special emphasis on the server-side API.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;He will also explain how it is so easy to implement your own UPnP devices using &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.gupnp.org/&#34;&gt;GUPnP&lt;/a&gt; with the help of an example Light Bulb device that implements two simple services. I will also explain why &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.gupnp.org/&#34;&gt;GUPnP&lt;/a&gt; deserves to be the default UPnP stack on maemo and GNOME platforms.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
